Now I smell flowers.
There is a small flower stall here.
The fragrance of the flowers is very nice.
An older woman is sitting there.
She is making a marigold garland.
The marigold flowers are very fresh.
I stop near the stall.
The aunty looks at me and smiles.
I do not ask her the price.
But she tells me the price on her own.
"Madam, take this fresh garland."
"It is for only twenty rupees."
I like that garland a lot.
It is nice for the door of my flat.
I happily say to her, "Aunty, give me one garland."
I take twenty rupees out of my purse.
I give her the money.
She gives me that beautiful garland.
I put it in my cloth bag.
